WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.650
VFX artist Didier Konings was hired to take
care of the little details in “The Conjuring

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:10.330
2” — and we mean little — removing security
cameras and altering buildings in minor ways

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:12.970
to make the 1970s setting look authentic.

00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:18.119
But despite these changes, there was nothing
retro about the camera setup that director

00:00:18.119 --> 00:00:19.460
James Wan used.

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:23.520
He opted to shoot in digital over film, explaining
in an interview to Collider:

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:28.349
"I used the Alexa on this one, the same camera
that I used on the first ‘Conjuring’ and

00:00:28.349 --> 00:00:31.320
also the same camera I used on ‘Fast and
Furious 7.’

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:36.950
I'm a big fan of the Alexa camera because
I think it just creates really beautiful blacks.”

